@prefix gmeow:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix skos:   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix semapv: <https://w3id.org/semapv/vocab/> .

# Term equivalences for the norms slice — GMEOW authoring source.
# Compiled to mappings/gmeow-norms.sssom.tsv by the mapping compiler.
#
# This set seeds NO alignment cells. Its two former cells aligned
# gmeow:assessmentTarget and gmeow:assessmentScoreValue to schema.org's review
# cluster; both properties are core-owned by the observations slice alongside
# gmeow:Assessment, and an alignment belongs to the slice that owns the term it
# aligns, so both cells now live in slices/core/observations/mappings/
# equivalences.ttl. The terms norms still owns (Norm, Duty, Persona, StyleGuide,
# the deontic and precedence machinery) have no stable external IRI vocabulary
# to map to; the same intentional prose-only shape the metacognition and inquiry
# slices apply.

gmeow:mapsetNorms a gmeow:MappingSet ;
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-norms.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:setId "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/mappings/norms" ;
    gmeow:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    gmeow:setComment "Norms-slice alignments are intentionally cell-free: the Assessment/rubric alignments to schema.org's review cluster ride gmeow:assessmentTarget and gmeow:assessmentScoreValue, which are core-owned by the observations slice, so they are authored there (mappings/equivalences.ttl) rather than re-mapped here — an alignment belongs to the slice that owns the term. The norms-owned deontic vocabulary (Norm, Duty, deonticModality, the precedence and persona machinery) has no stable external IRI vocabulary to align to.".
